  "articleBody": "Ever tripped over a stray cord or a pile of stuff in your kitchen? We've all been there, and it's super annoying, not to mention dangerous! Keeping your kitchen free from cords and clutter is a big part of preventing trips and falls. Here’s how you can make it safer. First, pay attention to where your appliance cords are running. Don't let them snake across walkways or high-traffic areas. Use cord organizers or clips to keep them neatly tucked away and off the floor. Next, tackle the clutter. It’s easy for things to accumulate, but storing items in paths is a big no-no. Find dedicated spots for everything, and make sure those high-traffic zones stay clear. Good lighting also plays a huge role; sometimes you just don't see that small obstacle. If you're finding that despite your best efforts, you're still dealing with hazards due to your kitchen's layout or design, or if you have permanent level changes that are tricky, HH Remodeling LLC can help you redesign your space for better flow and safety. We're happy to discuss your needs at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
